# Rank 1410 / CVE-2020-25020: mpxj reads Microsoft Project, Primavera,
# GanttProject, Gantt Designer, Phoenix and ConceptDraw project files, and six
# of its readers unmarshal the caller's stream through a SAX parser they build
# themselves. Four of them built it from a stock factory:
#
#   SAXParserFactory factory = SAXParserFactory.newInstance();
#   SAXParser saxParser = factory.newSAXParser();
#   XMLReader xmlReader = saxParser.getXMLReader();
#   SAXSource doc = new SAXSource(xmlReader, new InputSource(stream));
#   Project ganttProject = (Project) CONTEXT.createUnmarshaller().unmarshal(doc);
#
# A JAXP SAXParserFactory left in its default state processes DOCTYPE
# declarations and resolves external entities, so a `.gan`, `.ppx`, `.cdpz` or
# Gantt Designer file carrying
# `<!DOCTYPE p [<!ENTITY e SYSTEM "file:///etc/passwd">]>` makes the library
# read local files and fetch attacker-chosen URLs on behalf of whatever opened
# the project file -- CWE-611, GHSA-wcp5-m52f-mhh5.
#
# Step 0, `commit?` / metadata COMMIT_MISMATCH: the row is correct. Pool SHA
# 0d830e8cbe5213968abb1bcb1c816ca2ee00aa53 resolves in joniles/mpxj as "XXE
# vulnerability fix (#178)", 29 Aug 2020, and it is the fixing change rather than a
# release bump: it adds net/sf/mpxj/common/UnmarshalHelper.java, whose
# createXmlReader() sets
# `factory.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/disallow-doctype-decl", true)`
# before newSAXParser(), and rewrites all seven XML readers to route through it.
# The remediation is present at the fixed revision (the only SAXParserFactory left in
# src/main/java is UnmarshalHelper's, hardened) and the vulnerable construct is
# present at the parent: of seven `factory.newSAXParser()` sites at
# 0d830e8cbe^, PhoenixReader:138, ConceptDrawProjectReader:117,
# GanttDesignerReader:99 and GanttProjectReader:141 set no feature at all, while
# MSPDIReader:197, PlannerReader:133 and PrimaveraPMFileReader:269
# disallowed doctype declarations. No pool row correction.
#
# The construct is bound and the rule for it exists: binding xmlParserCreate143
# labels `newSAXParser` code.XmlParserCreate and VYQL-DESER-004 judges it
# medium unless a core.XmlHardening control covers the site. Scanning the four
# unhardened readers on their own at 0d830e8cbe^ reports all four, with
# `unless endpoint coveredBy core.XmlHardening` and
# `unless sameReceiver coveredBy core.XmlHardening` both unsatisfied, and the
# fixed forms of the same seven files plus UnmarshalHelper report none.
#
# On the real tree the four findings were suppressed, and the cause was the
# receiver-name fallback behind `unless sameReceiver coveredBy
# core.XmlHardening`. `Engine.sameReceiverGuardReceivers`
# (internal/engine/engine.go) folded every guard node carrying concrete
# `sameReceiver` coverage into one map keyed on the receiver's identifier text,
# cached per control and qualified by neither file, package, function nor type,
# and `Engine.sameReceiverGuarded` consulted it by name whenever the sink's own
# `recv` node carries no coverage. Every one of the seven readers spells its
# factory local `factory`, so MSPDIReader's one setFeature call cleared the four
# unhardened readers in other packages; MerlinReader survived only because its
# receiver chain is `DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance`, a different name. The
# fallback now keys a guard by its receiver's name within the guard's own file,
# so a same-named local in another file no longer inherits the coverage, while a
# receiver hardened in a constructor or initialiser still covers its uses
# elsewhere in the same file -- the idiom the fallback exists for.
#
# Measured on the real tree: scanning src/main/java whole at 0d830e8cbe^
# reports five VYQL-DESER-004 -- PhoenixReader:138,
# ConceptDrawProjectReader:117, GanttDesignerReader:99, GanttProjectReader:141
# and the untouched MerlinReader:169 -- stably over three runs, and the fixed
# revision reports only MerlinReader:169. VYQL-DESER-002 stays at 49 rows on
# the parent and the finding total moves 401 to 405, exactly the four recovered
# rows and nothing else. On lucene/queryparser, the tree where the fallback was
# first measured, the parent revision's nine rows are byte-identical before and
# after, and the fixed revision goes from four rows to eight: the four that
# return are the byte-identical unhardened constructions the upstream fix never
# touched, and the only row the revision pair still removes is
# CoreParser.java:137, the line that fix itself hardened.
#
# The last three cases below are the minimal pairs. The cross-file pair -- a
# hardened reader and a stock reader, both locals named factory, one file each
# -- differs from the same-file pair only in where the classes live, and that is
# the only token that decides. Within one file the name-keyed approximation
# still covers, deliberately, so a same-named local in the hardening's own file
# stays silenced: the residual the same-file pair pins, and the reason the
# unhardened local's name is the token the last pair varies.
#
# Two precision defects showed up in the same revision pair and are recorded
# rather than fixed here. Binding xmlParse141 is `callee.method == "parse"` with
# no receiver constraint, so of 49 VYQL-DESER-002 (CWE-611, high) rows on
# src/main/java at 0d830e8cbe^, 46 are `DateFormat`/`DecimalFormat`/
# `NumberFormat.parse` calls in DatatypeConverter and Record classes and two are
# mpxj's own private `parse(...)` helpers. And VYQL-DESER-002 cannot separate
# these revisions in either direction: its three real `XMLFilter.parse` rows are
# ConceptDrawProjectReader:131 (genuinely vulnerable), MSPDIReader:229 and
# PrimaveraPMFileReader:284 (both hardened), and at the fixed revision the row
# simply moves to the hardened UnmarshalHelper.java:101.
#
# verify_current_expected: fixed
#
# The binding and rule predate the fix and are unchanged; only the engine's
# receiver-key scoping moved. OWASP Java and Python are gated on the stacked
# branch with the engine change in place.

test "rank1410: GanttProjectReader unmarshals the caller's stream through a stock SAXParserFactory"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/net/sf/mpxj/ganttproject/GanttProjectReader.java
  expect VYQL-DESER-004
  code
  ```
  package net.sf.mpxj.ganttproject;

  import java.io.InputStream;

  import javax.xml.bind.JAXBContext;
  import javax.xml.bind.Unmarshaller;
  import javax.xml.parsers.SAXParser;
  import javax.xml.parsers.SAXParserFactory;
  import javax.xml.transform.sax.SAXSource;

  import org.xml.sax.InputSource;
  import org.xml.sax.XMLReader;

  import net.sf.mpxj.ProjectFile;
  import net.sf.mpxj.ganttproject.schema.Project;

  public final class GanttProjectReader extends AbstractProjectReader
  {
     @Override public ProjectFile read(InputStream stream) throws MPXJException
     {
        try
        {
           m_projectFile = new ProjectFile();
           m_eventManager = m_projectFile.getEventManager();

           m_projectFile.getProjectProperties().setFileApplication("GanttProject");
           m_projectFile.getProjectProperties().setFileType("GAN");

           m_eventManager.addProjectListeners(m_projectListeners);

           SAXParserFactory factory = SAXParserFactory.newInstance();
           SAXParser saxParser = factory.newSAXParser();
           XMLReader xmlReader = saxParser.getXMLReader();
           SAXSource doc = new SAXSource(xmlReader, new InputSource(stream));

           if (CONTEXT == null)
           {
              throw CONTEXT_EXCEPTION;
           }

           Unmarshaller unmarshaller = CONTEXT.createUnmarshaller();

           Project ganttProject = (Project) unmarshaller.unmarshal(doc);

           readProjectProperties(ganttProject);
           readTasks(ganttProject);

           return m_projectFile;
        }

        catch (Exception ex)
        {
           throw new MPXJException("Failed to parse file", ex);
        }
     }

     private ProjectFile m_projectFile;
     private EventManager m_eventManager;
     private static final JAXBContext CONTEXT;
     private static JAXBException CONTEXT_EXCEPTION;
  }
  ```

test "rank1410: the fixed revision builds every reader's XMLReader from a factory that disallows doctype declarations"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/net/sf/mpxj/common/UnmarshalHelper.java
  reject VYQL-DESER-004
  code
  ```
  package net.sf.mpxj.common;

  import java.io.InputStream;

  import javax.xml.bind.JAXBContext;
  import javax.xml.parsers.ParserConfigurationException;
  import javax.xml.parsers.SAXParserFactory;
  import javax.xml.transform.sax.SAXSource;

  import org.xml.sax.InputSource;
  import org.xml.sax.SAXException;
  import org.xml.sax.XMLReader;

  public final class UnmarshalHelper
  {
     public static final Object unmarshal(JAXBContext context, InputStream stream) throws SAXException, ParserConfigurationException
     {
        return context.createUnmarshaller().unmarshal(new SAXSource(createXmlReader(), new InputSource(stream)));
     }

     public static final XMLReader createXmlReader() throws SAXException, ParserConfigurationException
     {
        SAXParserFactory factory = SAXParserFactory.newInstance();
        factory.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/disallow-doctype-decl", true);
        factory.setNamespaceAware(true);
        return factory.newSAXParser().getXMLReader();
     }
  }
  ```

test "rank1410: the patched reader builds no parser of its own"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/net/sf/mpxj/ganttproject/GanttProjectReader.java
  reject VYQL-DESER-004
  code
  ```
  package net.sf.mpxj.ganttproject;

  import java.io.InputStream;

  import javax.xml.bind.JAXBContext;

  import net.sf.mpxj.ProjectFile;
  import net.sf.mpxj.common.UnmarshalHelper;
  import net.sf.mpxj.ganttproject.schema.Project;

  public final class GanttProjectReader extends AbstractProjectReader
  {
     @Override public ProjectFile read(InputStream stream) throws MPXJException
     {
        try
        {
           if (CONTEXT == null)
           {
              throw CONTEXT_EXCEPTION;
           }

           m_projectFile = new ProjectFile();
           m_eventManager = m_projectFile.getEventManager();

           m_projectFile.getProjectProperties().setFileApplication("GanttProject");
           m_projectFile.getProjectProperties().setFileType("GAN");

           m_eventManager.addProjectListeners(m_projectListeners);

           Project ganttProject = (Project) UnmarshalHelper.unmarshal(CONTEXT, stream);

           readProjectProperties(ganttProject);
           readTasks(ganttProject);

           return m_projectFile;
        }

        catch (Exception ex)
        {
           throw new MPXJException("Failed to parse file", ex);
        }
     }

     private ProjectFile m_projectFile;
     private EventManager m_eventManager;
     private static final JAXBContext CONTEXT;
     private static JAXBException CONTEXT_EXCEPTION;
  }
  ```

test "rank1410: a sibling reader that hardens its own factory silences one that does not, because both locals are named factory"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/net/sf/mpxj/mspdi/MSPDIReader.java
  reject VYQL-DESER-004
  code
  ```
  package net.sf.mpxj.mspdi;

  import java.io.InputStream;

  import javax.xml.parsers.SAXParser;
  import javax.xml.parsers.SAXParserFactory;
  import javax.xml.transform.sax.SAXSource;

  import org.xml.sax.InputSource;
  import org.xml.sax.XMLReader;

  public final class MSPDIReader
  {
     public XMLReader hardenedReader() throws Exception
     {
        SAXParserFactory factory = SAXParserFactory.newInstance();
        factory.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/disallow-doctype-decl", true);
        factory.setNamespaceAware(true);
        SAXParser saxParser = factory.newSAXParser();
        return saxParser.getXMLReader();
     }
  }

  final class GanttProjectReader
  {
     public SAXSource sourceFor(InputStream stream) throws Exception
     {
        SAXParserFactory factory = SAXParserFactory.newInstance();
        SAXParser saxParser = factory.newSAXParser();
        XMLReader xmlReader = saxParser.getXMLReader();
        return new SAXSource(xmlReader, new InputSource(stream));
     }
  }
  ```

test "rank1410: renaming the unhardened factory's local, and nothing else, restores the finding"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/net/sf/mpxj/mspdi/MSPDIReader.java
  expect VYQL-DESER-004
  code
  ```
  package net.sf.mpxj.mspdi;

  import java.io.InputStream;

  import javax.xml.parsers.SAXParser;
  import javax.xml.parsers.SAXParserFactory;
  import javax.xml.transform.sax.SAXSource;

  import org.xml.sax.InputSource;
  import org.xml.sax.XMLReader;

  public final class MSPDIReader
  {
     public XMLReader hardenedReader() throws Exception
     {
        SAXParserFactory factory = SAXParserFactory.newInstance();
        factory.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/disallow-doctype-decl", true);
        factory.setNamespaceAware(true);
        SAXParser saxParser = factory.newSAXParser();
        return saxParser.getXMLReader();
     }
  }

  final class GanttProjectReader
  {
     public SAXSource sourceFor(InputStream stream) throws Exception
     {
        SAXParserFactory plainFactory = SAXParserFactory.newInstance();
        SAXParser saxParser = plainFactory.newSAXParser();
        XMLReader xmlReader = saxParser.getXMLReader();
        return new SAXSource(xmlReader, new InputSource(stream));
     }
  }
  ```

